Package: glyph
Title: A Grammar of Interactive Graphics
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Joash Joshua", "Ayo", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "joashjoshua789@gmail.com"),
    person("Mike", "Bostock", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
    comment = "Author of the bundled D3.js library"))
Description: Builds interactive graphics from a declarative specification.
    Marks, scales, tooltips, zoom, brushing, linked selections, animated
    transitions and multi-plot layouts are declared in one pipeline and
    stored as a plain R list that can be inspected, saved as JSON or
    converted to 'Vega-Lite'. Plots are drawn in the browser with 'D3.js'
    and work at the console, in R Markdown and 'Quarto' documents, and in
    'Shiny' apps, where brushed selections are returned to R.
